# Merge attributes for the factory's conflict pass (ADR-0103).
#
# worktree-cli.mjs merge-main passes this file to `git merge` with
# `-c core.attributesFile=<this file>`, so it applies whatever the PR branch
# carries: an old branch has no .gitattributes of its own. The union driver
# keeps every line both sides added, so two PRs that each appended a row to the
# ADR index merge cleanly instead of stopping the merge for a Claude run.
# merge-main passes it only when a preview merge of the index conflicts on
# index rows alone: on any other line union would keep both wordings. It then
# checks the result for an ADR listed twice.
docs/adr/README.md merge=union
